aims-os-centre-senegal-labo (2.1+4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Hardening against the student at the keyboard: GRUB superuser
    (/etc/grub.d/01_aims_labo_password reads a hash written on the
    golden machine by aims-labo-grub-password; Debian's 10_linux
    diverted and patched with --unrestricted so normal boot needs no
    password), the installer's local sudo account locked and removed
    from sudo, NetworkManager actions reserved to administrators
    (polkit rule). Sudo for IT comes from the directory (admins).

